{
 "name": "button_pad",
 "description": "13x13 SWCH/HSWC checkerboard button, headed by a WIFI channel cell and a PSCN/NSCN pad.",
 "why": "Console button pattern (build-lessons 'control console pattern'): a WIFI channel receiver over a PSCN (or NSCN) pad drives a checkerboard of SWCH/HSWC so a spark on the column fans out across the whole pad instead of one pixel, giving a big, reliably-triggered button per channel. v2 hardening: WIFI was fully unjacketed (blueprint_lint heat_source_uninsulated). Widened WIFI by 1 column (away from the PSCN it touches) so a full INSL ring wraps it while the original PSCN contact -- the actual signal entry -- stays touching WIFI exactly as captured. Re-verified: blueprint_lint reports zero critical findings, compile ok.",
 "source": "save2, x251-263 y45-61 (one of four pads, x176-330 y28-62)",
